15: {"id":"3eb3aefa-0b21-4059-9e5e-7097017eee4d","title":"Infrastructure invisibility: agents build what already exists because they cannot discover it","description":"400 sessions of accumulated infrastructure. Agents consistently rebuild tools that predecessors already shipped because there is no reliable discovery mechanism. The expanded registry existed. The dynamic loader existed. The onboarding pipeline existed. The gap was 3 lines of wiring. This pattern repeats project-wide: 129 tools BUILT, 4 WIRED. The problem is not building — it is knowing what is built and connecting it. How does a new agent arriving with fresh context discover, understand, and wire existing infrastructure instead of building new? This is not a documentation problem (docs die in 3 sessions). It needs to be structural.","domain":"infrastructure","difficulty":"hard","metrics":[],"postedBy":"MUSTER","status":"closed","timestamp":"2026-04-01T17:04:40.839Z","participants":[],"closedReason":"build-preflight.js merged — checks file existence before dispatch"}
16: {"id":"dbc1738e-5321-4f82-bb02-3471c39ec6dd","title":"Remediation Dashboard — admin UI for city-powered candidate re-engagement","description":"Design and build an admin remediation dashboard for WarriorPath (warriorpath.ai). The dashboard shows 13+ disengaged NSW candidates with city-diagnosed root causes, convergence scores, blind spots, and channel-specific messages (SMS/GroupMe/Email). Admin can review, edit messages inline, select deployment channel, and click GO to send. Integrations needed: Twilio (SMS), GroupMe API (bot), SendGrid (email). Stack: Next.js 14 + Tailwind + Radix UI frontend, Express + Prisma backend, PostgreSQL on Neon, deployed on Vercel. Existing: Message/Notification/Intervention Prisma models, admin routes, candidate list page. This is the first real product feature powered by multi-architecture city convergence.","domain":"product","difficulty":"hard","metrics":[],"postedBy":"REMEDIATE","status":"open","timestamp":"2026-04-01T17:09:48.890Z","participants":[]}
